"""Authored rural/maritime opportunities; ordinary native quests own settlement."""
import collections,json,re

TYPES={
 'Tideglass Shrimp':'Thumb-sized transparent shrimp whose blue organs flash in bright rock pools. They graze on algae and retreat into cracks; a panicked group can spoil delicate samples without becoming a lethal swarm.',
 'Brinecap Slime':'A small low dome of salty translucent jelly carrying a cap of trapped foam. It follows mineral runoff, clings to nets and stings bare skin; fresh water and a suitable container can redirect it.',
 'Inkpot Cuttlefish':'A clever, hand-sized marine animal with a dark mantle and two broad silver eyes. It imitates the texture beneath it and squirts ink when cornered. It is an animal, not a secret speaking scholar.',
 'Hookbeak Gull':'A heavy white-and-gray gull with a curved rust-colored bill. It steals fish and glossy objects from open baskets and defends a nearby nest. Feeding, covering cargo or leaving its ledge can avoid a fight.',
 'Sailcloth Moth':'A cream-colored coastal moth with wing markings resembling tiny knots. Its larvae eat damp canvas and grain sacks; an adult scatters irritating powder. Finding the source matters more than swatting one moth.',
 'Kelpclaw Crab':'A squat green crab whose flat foreclaws collect strips of living kelp. It braces in the surf and snaps at hands reaching into its refuge. A stick, bait and sensible footwear are useful.',
 'Bellfin Shoal':'Small blue fish with hollow translucent fins that ring together when startled. A school can confuse shouted boat signals, but the fish ordinarily flee. Light and sound lure them in different directions.',
 'Shoalglass Ray':'A broad pale ray with translucent wing edges and a stony central spine. It rests beneath clear sand and discharges a short magical jolt when stepped on. A visible sand outline gives careful waders warning.',
 'Mooring Mimic':'A small mimic resembling a damp coil of rope with an attached wooden float. Its sticky underside grabs careless hands; tugging hard tightens it. It cannot imitate a whole vessel or read a person’s thoughts.',
 'Barnacle Brute':'A barrel-sized crustacean with two mismatched pincers and a back armored in pale barnacles. It scavenges flooded holds and pins loose timber across entrances. Moving its food can draw it away from a narrow passage.',
 'Undertow Eel':'A long dark-green eel with pale jointed jaw plates and a thin violet line along its flanks. It makes short pulling currents around wreck crevices. The current weakens away from its refuge; it cannot drag someone across the sea.',
 'Salt-Crest Wyvern':'A lean two-legged, two-winged coastal predator with salt-white head spines and a hooked tail. It circles exposed nesting rocks and takes fish or unattended catches. It is a wyvern, not a sacred speaking dragon.',
 'Reedlace Sprite':'A finger-length wingless plant creature with translucent seed-pod limbs and a fringe of reed leaves. It knots loose fishing line around warm stakes to build a shelter. Its mischievous behavior has a practical animal-like pattern rather than malicious omniscience.',
 'Tangletooth Otter':'A sleek brown otter with a pale throat and small branching ivory teeth. It collects tools that rattle and hides them in a dry bank. It can bite when cornered but prefers a chase to a fight.',
 'Burdock Lurker':'A low, six-legged woodland browser hidden beneath a coat of hooked seed burrs. It drags sacks and low cloth into its nest while foraging. Its blunt face and slow defensive roll distinguish it from a vicious wolf.',
 'Chalkback Ram':'A sturdy grassland sheep with pale stony plates along its spine and broad curling horns. A territorial adult knocks against carts and gates during the rut. Its lowered head and stamping hoof signal a charge before contact.'
}

# title, category, tier, value, slot, bonus(type,variable,value), natural text
