# name/client/place/level/rank/fee/public task/what counts/design
QUESTS=[
 ('Guild: The Mill Has Teeth','Shūhei Kusanagi','Wrenhill Windmill',1,1,35,'A grain sack keeps moving after the machinery stops. Shūhei needs the source removed without fouling the stones.','The stopped grinding floor is inspected and its finite flour-beetle infestation is removed or safely contained.','Use Flour Beetle, level 1–3, one modest encounter. Stop machinery first. Fuyuka suspects a worn chute, while Shūhei wants the sack blamed; the actual inspection can distinguish them. No lethal swarm or compulsory alchemy.'),
 ('Guild: A Ram in the Road','Rinako Matsuba','Longgrass Crossroads',3,1,40,'A chalk-backed ram is blocking a cart’s usual approach. Move it without breaking the cart or letting it into the crop plots.','The specific blocking ram is safely moved, restrained, deterred or defeated and the cart route is usable.','One Chalkback Ram, level 2–4, telegraphed charge. Bait, a barrier or Animal Handling can solve it. Its owner is careless rather than a hidden villain. Do not turn this into a whole monster cull.'),
 ('A Place before Supper','Tamae Shibano','Starlark Abbey',1,0,25,'The guest wing needs one usable room before a tired traveler arrives. A stuck shutter and damp bedding have made the obvious room unsuitable.','One agreed guest room is actually made usable with permission and the steward knows it is ready.','Finite practical work, not a mandatory profession tutorial. Tamae wants neat work but will accept a sensible temporary repair. A failure changes the method, not the amount of invented paperwork.'),
 ('Guild: Knots in the Reedwalk','Daisaku Minobe','Greenrush Estuary',4,1,45,'Loose lines are tangling the reedwalk supports. Find what is moving them and leave the landing usable.','The tangling cause is identified and the agreed passage restored without abandoning a trapped person or animal.','A small Reedlace Sprite colony is making shelter, not plotting murder. Relocating its useful material can work; careless burning damages the landing. Beginner local danger only.'),
 ('A Jar That Will Not Settle','Yorina Tsugawa','Thistlebank Alchemy Cottage',5,0,45,'One field preparation has begun separating in storage. Yorina wants a useful comparison before she sells the next batch.','A feasible comparison is carried out and the actual instability is explained honestly to Yorina.','A simple experiment or qualified helper suffices. A good result can be an ordinary storage defect; do not require a new spell or make every potion secretly cursed. Yorina dislikes bad news but values an answer she can use.'),
 ('Guild: Wings in the Stores','Nanae Kogure','The Gilded Albatross',7,1,70,'Damp sailcloth moths are spoiling the ship’s stores. Nanae wants the affected goods separated and the source dealt with.','The finite infestation and its damp source are dealt with, preserving a usable uncontaminated store.','Sailcloth Moth, level 5–8. Cleaning, isolation and drying are valid. Sōji argues for salvaging more stock; Nanae refuses to feed dubious grain to the crew. This is their real disagreement, not a scene staged for player approval.'),
 ('Guild: A Light beneath the Jetty','Saki Hinoura','Beaconrest Lighthouse',8,1,75,'Boat signals are being answered by strange little flashes under the lighthouse jetty. Saki needs a clear channel before the next supply arrival.','The false-signal source is established and a workable signaling arrangement is demonstrated.','Bellfin Shoal and reflected lantern light, not another portal anomaly. Observation, a shielded lamp or moving the fish can work. Kōzō’s familiar explanation is incomplete rather than malicious.'),
 ('Guild: Tools in the Bank','Daisaku Minobe','Greenrush Estuary',9,1,80,'A boatwright’s small tools have vanished near the bank. Recover them without ruining the unfinished hull.','The agreed missing tools are recovered or replaced by a genuinely accepted equivalent.','A Tangletooth Otter has collected rattling objects. A limited chase, lure or safe den approach works. The animal bites only when cornered; no boss-level otter surprise.'),
 ('The Wrong Kind of Hide','Uta Nekoyama','Pinewater Woods',10,0,90,'A poacher wants help recovering a hide before someone else finds her cache. The ownership of another item in it is less straightforward.','The agreed hide/cache problem is resolved through recovery, a negotiated settlement or truthful exposure of the disputed property.','Uta can be charming and selfish. Establish actual ownership before moving goods. Refusing the dishonest portion is a real choice, not automatic failure. A small Burdock Lurker or ordinary tracks can complicate the recovery without requiring combat.'),
 ('The Bell That Wakes the Ward','Eiji Kuramochi','Starlark Abbey',7,0,65,'A wind-shaken bell keeps interrupting the hospice. Eiji would like it quiet without damaging a cherished part of worship.','A practical safe fix reduces the nuisance and is accepted by those actually affected.','Chizuru cares about observance; Lucette about exhausted patients. Let the novice mediate a modest issue without deciding which faith is true. No hidden demon or compulsory Soul spell.'),
 ('Guild: A Rope with Opinions','Mio Tatsunami','The Gilded Albatross',12,1,105,'A suspicious coil recovered from a buoy has fastened itself around a working rail. Free the rail without tearing the deck fittings out.','The finite Mooring Mimic is removed or contained and the rail is usable.','One level 9–13 mimic, visible sticky grip and room to retreat. Daigo’s knot knowledge helps only if consulted. No instant inventory theft or attack on every crew member.'),
 ('Guild: The Mark below the Arch','Mina Takanashi','Moonarch Isle',15,2,145,'A low-tide carving may help identify the ruined arch’s original use. Record it before the undercroft floods.','The specified surviving carving is actually recorded with a sensible route and return, and usable evidence reaches the client.','Survey the Tide Crypt, tide and stable footing. Avoid a fabricated new realm or activation ritual. The inscription may describe a mundane harbor function. Useful negative findings can challenge Mina’s preferred theory.'),
 ('A Second Pair of Eyes','Brina Flintmere','Old Southwatch',13,0,120,'Brina and Yūsei want a usable coastal route checked from the old lookout. They disagree over how much of the exposed approach needs measuring.','A bounded agreed route is checked and its actual limitations recorded in usable form.','Hirotaka disputes a modern marker based on memory; evidence can vindicate or correct him. The partners keep their own argument. Do not require a dangerous sea dive merely to expose Brina’s private weakness.'),
 ('What the Shell Caught','Mina Takanashi','Stillback Isle',12,0,130,'Mauruun keeps shifting one edge of its shell. Mina suspects a small problem that could be investigated without hurting the enormous animal.','The actual source of discomfort is identified from a safe approach and a feasible care plan is agreed.','The level-60 turtle remains passive unless provoked. Patient observation and consent-like animal responses matter. Discover the trapped old line; no climbing into a furious fight or mandatory killing. Offer further care only after this finding.'),
 ('A Patient Kind of Work','Mina Takanashi','Stillback Isle',14,0,180,'Removing old line from Mauruun’s shell will take steady hands and a way to stop before the animal is distressed.','The trapped line is actually removed or an equally effective safe treatment carried out, relieving the identified irritation.','Build on What the Shell Caught. Ordinary tools, practiced animal care, Healing where applicable or a qualified helper can contribute. Nature does not automatically heal an animal. Stop or retreat when its response requires it. Do not tame it or promise a permanent mount.'),
 ('The Nesting Shelf','Makiho Akitsu','Stillback Isle',15,0,190,'Boats have been using Mauruun’s protected resting shelf as an easy landing. Find a workable way to keep traffic clear.','The affected landing users accept and begin a workable alternative that leaves the nesting shelf undisturbed.','Build on actual observation rather than stealing eggs to prove they exist. A better landing, notices and negotiation can end this peaceful arc. Makiho wants a usable fishing approach; Mina wants careful boundaries. No need to fight the turtle.'),
 ('Guild: A Hold Full of Knuckles','Iris Mornay','Splinterwake Wreck',20,2,230,'A wreck’s accessible hold contains recoverable goods and an obstructed exit. Agree the salvage scope and make a safe recovery.','The specific agreed cargo is recovered with a feasible dive, actual ownership arrangements and a usable way back.','A finite Barnacle Brute at level 17–22 can block the opening; lure, avoid or fight it. Air and exit routes matter. Ghorvath may be absent; its signs warn of optional much greater danger and do not force a boss fight.'),
 ('The Name on the Crate','Sōji Hamada','The Gilded Albatross',20,0,240,'Recovered cargo carries an old shipping mark and a newer private claim. Establish who can actually authorize its sale.','Relevant evidence is checked and the participating salvagers reach an actual defensible disposition of the disputed goods.','Build on the recovery, without requiring the player to have taken every possible wreck job. Reina needs a profitable recovery; Sōji wants a defensible sale. Kanna may offer a knowingly dubious shortcut. The claimant can be mistaken without a secret evil mastermind. Refusal, restitution or an informed limited settlement can resolve it; public disagreement remains possible.'),
 ('The Price of Bringing It Back','Reina Kazehara','The Gilded Albatross',23,0,280,'A valuable recovery will only become a success if the agreed cargo reaches its rightful destination and the crew’s promises survive the voyage.','The specifically agreed cargo is actually delivered or another informed settlement is carried out with those entitled to decide.','Close the salvage arc from the established ownership decision. Weather, an ordinary damaged fitting or a claimant’s changed terms can complicate one finite trip. Do not fabricate repeated betrayals. Remember actual crew shares privately, but the player receives the posted full agreed reward once.'),
 ('Guild: The Current in the Wall','Iris Mornay','Moonarch Isle',24,2,280,'An undercroft passage pulls harder than the tide should account for. Locate the cause before another survey crew uses it.','The local danger is identified and removed, contained or credibly marked with a workable safe route.','One Undertow Eel at level 20–26; observe its crevice and limited current range. A false wall or loose stones can be a mundane alternative cause. No forced deep-ocean boss.'),
 ('A Quiet View, Honestly','Kōzō Hinoura','Seaward Overlook',1,0,20,'A borrowed fieldglass has been left near the overlook. Return it without disturbing the people who went there for some peace.','The actual borrowed fieldglass is found and returned or its loss is honestly settled with the owner.','A brief quiet errand. No resident NPC is added to the overlook, no mandatory romance and no manufactured monster attack. A shy visitor can decline conversation.'),
 ('Guild: A Nest above the Catch','Makiho Akitsu','Gullwatch Reefs',27,2,320,'A salt-crested wyvern has begun taking catches from the outer ledges. Make the working approach usable without pretending the whole coast must be exterminated.','The particular affected approach is made usable by deterring, relocating, defeating or otherwise actually addressing the territorial animal.','One Salt-Crest Wyvern, level 24–30, visible circling and threatened nesting ground. Signpost the danger before a climb; preparation or partners help. An agreement about fishing times can work if its practical effect is demonstrated.'),
 ('The Bluecoil Watch','Mina Takanashi','Bluecoil Rest',30,0,380,'Nerathyl’s movements may explain why some boats approach safely while others wake the serpent. Carry out a cautious observation and identify a usable boundary.','A real observation establishes evidence for the animal’s behavior and a practical boundary is demonstrated or credibly communicated.','The fixed level-45 serpent begins asleep unless actual events changed that. Observe from the Distant Mooring. Naturally shed scales are possible finds; theft from its living body is provocation. No requirement to fight it, whisper a password or discover a human intelligence.'),
 ('Guild: Ghorvath at the Deepwater Edge','Reina Kazehara','Splinterwake Wreck',50,3,1600,'The kraken Ghorvath threatens the deep approaches. This is a deliberately dangerous hunt for a prepared company, not an ordinary salvage commission.','Ghorvath is actually defeated and no longer threatens the commissioned approaches through this individual’s attacks.','Explicitly warn that this is a level-55 boss hunt and select it only on a suitable or deliberately harder request. A preparation plan, seaworthy approach and real companions can help. Study, retreat or abandoning the uncompleted hunt remain valid. Do not summon a fresh kraken after its actual defeat or let a distant narration count as victory.')
]

def add(w):
    for name,desc in TYPES.items():
        assert name not in w['npcTypes'],name
        w['npcTypes'][name]={'name':name,'description':desc,'vulnerabilities':[],'resistances':[],'immunities':[]}
    for name,category,tier,value,slot,bonus,description in ITEMS:
        assert name not in w['itemTypes'],name
        item={'name':name,'category':category,'tier':tier,'estimatedValue':value,'description':description,'bonuses':[],'needsMediaGeneration':True}
        if slot:item['slot']=slot
        if bonus:item['bonuses']=[dict(zip(['type','variable','value'],bonus))]
        w['itemTypes'][name]=item
    qs=w['parties']['']['quests'];board=[]
    for name,client,place,level,rank,fee,public,outcome,design in QUESTS:
        assert name not in qs,name
        assert client in w['npcs'] and place in w['locations'],(name,client,place)
        brief=design+'\n\nOffer this finite work through the actual client or a relevant public notice. It starts only on actual agreement. Level guidance '+str(level)+'. '+('Minimum guild badge rank '+str(rank)+'. ' if rank else 'A personal commission, not a guild licence requirement. ')+f'The posted player reward is {fee} marks. The native completion effects are its sole payment and experience owner; narration does not add another purse. Settle the actual agreed outcome without mandatory return paperwork unless delivery or review itself matters. Preserve discoveries and losses if an approach fails. Use an achievable finite encounter and actual resources; do not scale named creatures or officials to manufacture an easy win. Newcomers can decline, postpone or withdraw.'
        qs[name]={'name':name,'questSource':client,'questLocation':place,'detailType':'detailed','status':'hidden','questStatement':public+f' Posted reward: {fee} marks.','mainObjective':outcome,'questDesignBrief':brief,'conclusive':True,'completionCondition':{'type':'story','query':'For the accepted undertaking '+name+', '+outcome+' The participating player has actually achieved that agreed outcome, not merely heard a rumor, stated an intention, observed someone else doing it or claimed a similar earlier success. Recognize a credible alternative that achieves the outcome without forcing the suggested method.'},'onCompleteEffects':[{'type':'item-add','item':'Mark','quantity':fee,'target':'allPlayers'},{'type':'player-experience','operator':'add','value':min(700,140+level*12),'target':'allPlayers'}]}
        if rank:
            qs[name]['onCompleteEffects'].append({'type':'item-add','item':'Guild Service Credit','quantity':1,'target':'allPlayers'})
            board.append([name,rank,'',False,level,'combat' if any(t in name for t in ['Ram','Teeth','Wings','Rope','Knuckles','Nest above','Ghorvath']) else 'other',1 if level<7 else 7 if level<15 else 15,client,place,fee])
    # Native offers chain significant developments, never independent reward monitors.
    for first,nextq in [('What the Shell Caught','A Patient Kind of Work'),('A Patient Kind of Work','The Nesting Shelf'),('Guild: A Hold Full of Knuckles','The Name on the Crate'),('The Name on the Crate','The Price of Bringing It Back')]:
        qs[first]['conclusive']=False
        qs[first]['onCompleteEffects'].append({'type':'quest-init','operator':'set','value':nextq})
    qs['A Patient Kind of Work']['onCompleteEffects'].append({'type':'item-add','item':'Stillback Shell Comb','quantity':1,'target':'allPlayers'})
    qs['The Nesting Shelf']['onCompleteEffects'].append({'type':'item-add','item':'Mauruun’s Shed Scute','quantity':1,'target':'allPlayers'})
    qs['Guild: Ghorvath at the Deepwater Edge']['onCompleteEffects'].append({'type':'item-add','item':'Ghorvath’s Beak Fragment','quantity':1,'target':'allPlayers'})
    # Match the live dispatcher's existing serialized array; keep its selection logic.
    t=w['triggerDefinitions']['gh_guild_board'];s=t['script'];m=re.search(r'const jobs=(\[.*?\])\.map',s,re.S)
    assert m,'Guild catalogue format changed; review instead of guessing'
    existing=json.loads(m[1]);rows=existing+board
    # The native trigger has a 10k text cap. Share repeated client/place strings;
    # decoded rows and all selection/acceptance behavior remain identical.
    counts=collections.Counter(row[i] for row in rows for i in [7,8])
    dictionary=[v for v,n in counts.items() if n>1];indexes={v:i for i,v in enumerate(dictionary)}
    encoded=[[indexes.get(v,v) if i in [7,8] else v for i,v in enumerate(row)] for row in rows]
    data=json.dumps(encoded,ensure_ascii=False,separators=(',',':'))
    decode=".map(r=>{for(const i of [7,8])if(typeof r[i]==='number')r[i]=ghxNames[r[i]];return r;})"
    s=s[:m.start(1)]+data+decode+s[m.end(1):]
    s='const ghxNames='+json.dumps(dictionary,ensure_ascii=False,separators=(',',':'))+';\n'+s
    brief="effects.push({type:'story',instruction:picked.length?'Offer only: '+picked.map(j=>j.title+' — '+j.client+'; '+j.place+'; '+j.fee+' marks (recommended level '+j.recommendedLevel+'+)').join('; ')+'. Give actual scope and wait for agreement. For deliberately requested harder work, explain its actual danger before agreement. Fresh terms and new work are required for a repeat. Browsing grants no acceptance, payment, credit, companion or portal permission. Other streets retain their own danger.':'No fitting fresh notice is selected. Preserve existing work and outcomes. If asked, propose a distinct suitable commission for the actual badge, travel permission and least experienced human; do not reopen a resolved crisis or substitute a high-level fight.'});"
    s,n=re.subn(r"effects.push\(\{type:'story',instruction:picked.length\?.*?\}\);",lambda _:brief,s,flags=re.S)
    assert n==1,'Board instruction format changed'
    t['script']=s
    # Personal clients use one local offer dispatcher, not unwritten flags or
    # a completion state machine. Follow-ups are owned by completion effects.
    followups={'A Patient Kind of Work','The Nesting Shelf','The Name on the Crate','The Price of Bringing It Back'}
    local=[[name,client,place,w['npcs'][client]['currentLocation']] for name,client,place,*_ in QUESTS if not name.startswith('Guild:') and name not in followups]
    w['triggerDefinitions'].pop('ghx_local_commissions',None)
    for i,(title,client,destination,home) in enumerate(local):
        name='ghx_local_commissions'+('' if i==0 else '_'+str(i+1))
        places=list(dict.fromkeys([destination,home]))
        location={'type':'party-location','operator':'equals','value':places[0]} if len(places)==1 else {'type':'party-location','operator':'regex','value':'^('+ '|'.join(re.escape(p) for p in places)+')$'}
        query=f'The player deliberately asks {client} about {title}, asks that actual client for suitable local work, or investigates the actual notice for {title}. The real client or notice is involved here. A greeting, arrival, rumor alone, unrelated business or another person’s completed job does not qualify.'
        w['triggerDefinitions'][name]={'name':name,'recurring':True,'scope':'party','conditions':[{'type':'party-realm','operator':'equals','value':'Glowhaven'},location,{'type':'quest-status','questId':title,'operator':'equals','value':'hidden'},{'type':'action','query':query}],'effects':[{'type':'quest-init','operator':'set','value':title},{'type':'story','instruction':f'Offer {title} through {client} or its real local notice. Explain its public situation and stated reward, then wait for acceptance or refusal. Destination: {destination}. This offer grants no acceptance, payment, licence, recruitment or completed work.'}],'script':"const tick=Number(check({type:'game-tick'}))||0;if(storage.ghxOfferTick===tick){skip=true}else{storage.ghxOfferTick=tick}"}
    # Keep these design arcs as linked native questlines. Two more global arc
    # surfacing checks exceeded the conservative Crucible budget (17 vs 15).
    # Do not rewrite unrelated old tournament or Spider triggers to make room.
    arcs={}
